# Phase 12 / Step 3 -- Channel-selective LACN (Hue-only)

OOD cohort: PAD-UFES-20, N = 200
Prevalence: 50.0% malignant

## Reuse Otsu masks from Step 2: reliable=172/200

Target Hue (circular mean over Phase 9 analytical sample): 359.08 deg

Hue-LACN applied (reliable mask): 172/200
Mean dP_hue_lacn (Hue-LACN - original P): +0.0531

Calibration: N=100 (pos=50, neg=50)
Test:        N=100 (pos=50, neg=50)

## Threshold recalibration on calibration
  Target recall: 0.79
  tau* (largest tau with recall >= 0.79) = 0.650  (cal recall=0.800, cal spec=0.500).

## Hue-only LACN test-set evaluation (N=100)
  AUC (no LACN): 0.8500
  AUC (Hue-LACN):0.7384

  (A) No LACN  + tau=0.661  : recall=0.820  spec=0.720  prec=0.745  f1=0.781  TP=41 FN=9 TN=36 FP=14
  (B) Hue LACN + tau=0.661  : recall=0.800  spec=0.520  prec=0.625  f1=0.702  TP=40 FN=10 TN=26 FP=24
  (C) Hue LACN + tau_LACN   : recall=0.820  spec=0.520  prec=0.631  f1=0.713  TP=41 FN=9 TN=26 FP=24

## Lab-LACN (Step 2) test-set comparison (same test split)
  tau_LACN_Lab (re-derived from calibration): 0.670
  AUC (Lab-LACN): 0.7984

  (A) No LACN  + tau=0.661 : recall=0.820  spec=0.720  f1=0.781
  (B) Lab LACN + tau=0.661 : recall=0.860  spec=0.600  f1=0.761
  (C) Lab LACN + tau_LACN  : recall=0.840  spec=0.640  f1=0.764

## Head-to-head: recalibrated C-Hue vs C-Lab vs A-baseline
  Recall    : A=0.820  C-Lab=0.840  C-Hue=0.820
  Specificity: A=0.720  C-Lab=0.640  C-Hue=0.520
  F1        : A=0.781  C-Lab=0.764  C-Hue=0.713
  AUC       : 0.850 (none)  0.798 (Lab)  0.738 (Hue)

## Verdict
  Hue-only LACN does not outperform Lab-LACN on the held-out test. The Lab-LACN trade-off appears to extend to Hue-only -- legitimate OOD color cues may live across multiple channels.

